  "openWorldHint": false,
  "readOnlyHint": true,
  "title": "List Chain Daddy's launch options"
 },
 "description": "Chain Daddy's launchpad and what it pays, per chain. The launchpad (`chaindaddy-launchpad`) creates the token together with its own locked trading pool, on EVM chains and on Solana (Meteora DBC): nothing up front, and the token's registration is free. For each chain: whether it can launch now (`launchable`), the contract the token ends up in, and the trading-fee economics in basis points of volume (`traderFeeBps` what traders pay, `creatorBps` what reaches the creator, `chainDaddyBps`). Chain Daddy's cut is set by the creator's plan when the token launches and fixed for that token (20% free, 15% annual Pro/Pro+/Developer, 5% annual Partner/Enterprise); these figures are the free plan's. For a plain token with no pool, Chain Daddy's token factory (`chaindaddy-classic`, a one-time fee with the registration included) is the other option.",
 "inputSchema": {
